### ═══════════════════════════════════════════════════════════════════
### Authorization workflow — org admin ▸ office admin ▸ occupant
###
### Schema:
###   organization  manage = admin
###   office        view   = admin + occupant + organization->manage
###                 manage = admin + organization->manage
###
### Actors (org "workflowco"):
###   • Fran  — founder ⇒ ORG admin
###   • Adam  — promoted to OFFICE admin of HQ (by Fran, the org admin)
###   • Otto  — plain occupant of HQ (added by Adam, the office admin)
###
### Rules verified:
###   • only org admin creates offices        (Adam create → 403, Fran → 201)
###   • org admin makes a user office admin    (Fran promote Adam → 204)
###   • office admin CAN add members           (Adam add Otto → 201)
###   • only ORG admin can promote to admin    (Adam promote Otto → 403)
###   • occupant cannot manage                 (Otto add/delete → 403)
###   • view: admin, occupant, org admin        (all GET → 200)
###   • only org admin deletes the org          (Otto → 403, Fran → 204)
###
### Self-contained. Run top-to-bottom. Requires the app up with
### orgcraft.spicedb.enabled=true and SpiceDB reachable — with SpiceDB
### disabled the permit-all fallback lets every check pass, so the 403s
### won't happen and the assertions become meaningless.
### NOTE: SpiceDB tuples are written by async module-event listeners, so
###       let each write settle before the verifying read (top-to-bottom
###       manual execution is plenty).
### ═══════════════════════════════════════════════════════════════════

@host = http://127.0.0.1:8080
@wfSlug = workflowco
@franEmail = fran@workflowco.com
@wfPassword = Password@123
@adamEmail = adam@workflowco.com
@ottoEmail = otto@workflowco.com

### V1. Register org (public) → Fran becomes ORG admin
POST {{host}}/api/v1/organizations
Content-Type: application/json

{
  "name": "WorkflowCo",
  "slug": "{{wfSlug}}",
  "founderFirstName": "Fran",
  "founderLastName": "Founder",
  "founderEmail": "{{franEmail}}",
  "founderPassword": "{{wfPassword}}"
}

> {%
    client.global.set("wfOrgId", response.body.organizationId);
    client.log("wfOrgId=" + response.body.organizationId);
%}

### V2. Login as Fran (org admin)
POST {{host}}/login
Content-Type: application/x-www-form-urlencoded

email={{franEmail}}&password={{wfPassword}}&tenant={{wfSlug}}

### V3. Create Adam (future office admin)
POST {{host}}/api/v1/users
Content-Type: application/json

{ "firstName": "Adam", "lastName": "Admin", "email": "{{adamEmail}}", "password": "{{wfPassword}}" }

> {% client.global.set("adamId", response.body.id); client.log("adamId=" + response.body.id); %}

### V4. Create Otto (future occupant)
POST {{host}}/api/v1/users
Content-Type: application/json

{ "firstName": "Otto", "lastName": "Occupant", "email": "{{ottoEmail}}", "password": "{{wfPassword}}" }

> {% client.global.set("ottoId", response.body.id); client.log("ottoId=" + response.body.id); %}

### V5. Fran (org admin) creates office HQ → 201
POST {{host}}/api/v1/offices
Content-Type: application/json

{ "name": "HQ Office", "address": { "address": "Via Roma 1", "city": "Rome", "country": "Italy" } }

> {%
    client.test("Org admin creates office", function () { client.assert(response.status === 201, "expected 201, got " + response.status); });
    client.global.set("officeId", response.body.id);
    client.log("officeId=" + response.body.id);
%}

### V6. Fran adds Adam as occupant of HQ → 201 (org admin can add members)
POST {{host}}/api/v1/offices/{{officeId}}/members
Content-Type: application/json

{ "officeId": "{{officeId}}", "userId": "{{adamId}}" }

> {% client.test("Org admin adds Adam", function () { client.assert(response.status === 201, "expected 201, got " + response.status); }); %}

### V7. Fran promotes Adam to OFFICE admin → 204 (only org admin may promote)
PUT {{host}}/api/v1/offices/{{officeId}}/members/{{adamId}}/admin

> {% client.test("Org admin promotes Adam to office admin", function () { client.assert(response.status === 204, "expected 204, got " + response.status); }); %}

### V8. Fran lists offices → sees HQ via organization->manage (1)
GET {{host}}/api/v1/offices

> {%
    client.test("Org admin sees HQ through the org hierarchy", function () {
        client.assert(response.status === 200, "status was " + response.status);
        client.assert(response.body.length === 1, "expected 1, got " + response.body.length);
        client.assert(response.body[0].id === client.global.get("officeId"), "should be HQ");
    });
%}

### ── As Adam (OFFICE admin of HQ) ───────────────────────────────────

### V9. Login as Adam
POST {{host}}/login
Content-Type: application/x-www-form-urlencoded

email={{adamEmail}}&password={{wfPassword}}&tenant={{wfSlug}}

### V10. Adam lists offices → sees HQ (admin ⇒ view) (1)
GET {{host}}/api/v1/offices

> {%
    client.test("Office admin sees HQ", function () {
        client.assert(response.status === 200, "status was " + response.status);
        client.assert(response.body.length === 1, "expected 1, got " + response.body.length);
    });
%}

### V11. Adam adds Otto as occupant → 201  ← office admin CAN add members
POST {{host}}/api/v1/offices/{{officeId}}/members
Content-Type: application/json

{ "officeId": "{{officeId}}", "userId": "{{ottoId}}" }

> {% client.test("Office admin adds a member", function () { client.assert(response.status === 201, "expected 201, got " + response.status); }); %}

### V12. Adam tries to promote Otto to admin → 403  ← only ORG admin may promote
PUT {{host}}/api/v1/offices/{{officeId}}/members/{{ottoId}}/admin

> {% client.test("Office admin CANNOT promote", function () { client.assert(response.status === 403, "expected 403, got " + response.status); }); %}

### V13. Adam tries to create another office → 403 (office admin is not org admin)
POST {{host}}/api/v1/offices
Content-Type: application/json

{ "name": "Branch Office", "address": { "address": "Via Milano 2", "city": "Milan", "country": "Italy" } }

> {% client.test("Office admin CANNOT create offices", function () { client.assert(response.status === 403, "expected 403, got " + response.status); }); %}

### ── As Otto (plain occupant of HQ) ─────────────────────────────────

### V14. Login as Otto
POST {{host}}/login
Content-Type: application/x-www-form-urlencoded

email={{ottoEmail}}&password={{wfPassword}}&tenant={{wfSlug}}

### V15. Otto views HQ → 200 (occupant ⇒ view)
GET {{host}}/api/v1/offices/{{officeId}}

> {% client.test("Occupant views HQ", function () { client.assert(response.status === 200, "got " + response.status); }); %}

### V16. Otto lists offices → sees HQ (1)
GET {{host}}/api/v1/offices

> {%
    client.test("Occupant sees HQ", function () {
        client.assert(response.status === 200, "status was " + response.status);
        client.assert(response.body.length === 1, "expected 1, got " + response.body.length);
    });
%}

### V17. Otto tries to add a member → 403 (occupant has no manage)
POST {{host}}/api/v1/offices/{{officeId}}/members
Content-Type: application/json

{ "officeId": "{{officeId}}", "userId": "{{adamId}}" }

> {% client.test("Occupant CANNOT add members", function () { client.assert(response.status === 403, "expected 403, got " + response.status); }); %}

### V18. Otto tries to delete HQ → 403 (occupant ≠ manage)
DELETE {{host}}/api/v1/offices/{{officeId}}

> {% client.test("Occupant CANNOT delete the office", function () { client.assert(response.status === 403, "expected 403, got " + response.status); }); %}

### V19. Otto tries to delete the org → 403 (not org admin)
DELETE {{host}}/api/v1/organizations/{{wfOrgId}}

> {% client.test("Occupant CANNOT delete the org", function () { client.assert(response.status === 403, "expected 403, got " + response.status); }); %}

### ── Teardown (only org admin may delete the org) ───────────────────

### V20. Login as Fran (org admin)
POST {{host}}/login
Content-Type: application/x-www-form-urlencoded

email={{franEmail}}&password={{wfPassword}}&tenant={{wfSlug}}

### V21. Fran deletes the org → 204. Cascades: HQ office + all org tuples removed.
DELETE {{host}}/api/v1/organizations/{{wfOrgId}}

> {% client.test("Org admin deletes the org", function () { client.assert(response.status === 204, "expected 204, got " + response.status); }); %}
